From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 9 Jul 2026 19:47:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ports/arkweb: vendor the arkweb-test app + a HAP build script

The pytest smoke tests drive a specific OpenHarmony app (bundle
org.openharmonyrs.arkwebtest) whose pages -- DialogPage, SplitPage,
TabsPage, the `--ps page` routing, the browser chrome -- are exactly what
the tests target. That app lived in a separate repo with the
port-specific changes uncommitted, splitting each feature (e.g. JS
dialogs: shim + test here, DialogPage there) across two repos. Vendor its
source under ports/arkweb/test-app so the shim, its test pages and the
tests version together and a checkout is self-sufficient to build, deploy
and test.

Vendored: the ArkTS/resources/config source (~240 KB) plus the public
OpenHarmony debug signing certs so the HAP signs out of the box. Build
outputs, oh_modules, .hvigor, local.properties and the 12 MB
hap-sign-tool.jar (located in the SDK toolchain) stay ignored.

Add ports/arkweb/tools/build_test_app.py to automate the HAP recipe
(local.properties, temporary SDK 26->21, clear signingConfigs -> unsigned
build, sign with the vendored certs, install), restoring
build-profile.json5 afterwards.

Verified on rk3568: build_test_app.py builds+signs+installs, and the six
dialog tests pass against the vendored-built app.

Validation: Test by running uv run ports/arkweb/tools/build_test_app.py (builds, signs and installs the HAP).
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; implementation and on-device testing)
